title: Fake CAPTCHA with a clipboard command
severity: critical
score: 80
tags: clickfix
attack: T1204.004, T1059.001, T1218.005
description: A fake CAPTCHA / verification page wrote a command to the clipboard, or did so
  with Run-dialog instructions. When genuine Turnstile/reCAPTCHA resources loaded,
  verification wording alone is not enough: it then needs Run-dialog instructions or an
  unambiguous ClickFix trait.
---
// A clipboard command ...
clipboard_commands
// ... with paste-into-Run steps, or on a page with verification wording. When a real
// CAPTCHA provider loaded, the wording alone is not enough: the command must then have
// an unambiguous ClickFix trait.
| where exists(run_dialog_pages)
    or (exists(verification_texts)
        and (toscalar(clipboard_commands | where trait == "unambiguous" | count) > 0
            or not(exists(genuine_challenge_requests))))
| project command = substring(text, 0, 1000), trait, frame_url
